cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PyMAPF: a Python framework for multi-agent planning and pathfinding"
message: >-
  If you use PyMAPF in your work, please cite the software using the metadata
  below. The survey it grew out of is listed under references.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lejeune
    given-names: Erwin
  - family-names: Sarkar
    given-names: Sampreet
repository-code: "https://github.com/openplan-labs/pymapf"
url: "https://openplan-labs.github.io/pymapf/"
abstract: >-
  A Python framework for multi-agent planning and pathfinding, written to be
  built upon and to explain the algorithms it implements. Centralized solvers
  include conflict-based search, weighted CBS, PIBT, LaCAM, large
  neighbourhood search, SIPP and space-time A*; decentralized control includes
  nonlinear model predictive control, velocity obstacles and swarm behaviours.
  The solver core is pure standard library and also runs in the browser.
license: MIT
version: 0.9.0
keywords:
  - multi-agent pathfinding
  - motion planning
  - robotics
  - conflict-based search
  - swarm
  - education
references:
  - type: report
    title: "Survey of the Multi-Agent Pathfinding Solutions"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lejeune
        given-names: Erwin
      - family-names: Sarkar
        given-names: Sampreet
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.13140/RG.2.2.14030.28486
    url: "https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.2.14030.28486"
